  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID/Liberia Improved Access to Safe Drinking Water in Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Liberia):  A new USAID mechanism will be.awarded in Q4 of FY 2022 with a focus on improving the access to and the use and.sustainability of basic drinking water services in Montserrado and Margibi.counties. The activity is focused on improving the management and increasing.the sustainability of existing water services in these two counties, while.ensuring that people currently using unimproved water sources gain access to a.basic level of drinking water services. .Using FY 2022 funds, the new activity will 1) strengthen the institutional.capacity of the counties to plan, budget, and oversee water services, including.improving policies, regulations, capacity, and coordination; 2) improve and.expand water service delivery through improved service delivery models,.capacity-building of water service providers, and ensuring inclusive water.services for poor and marginalized households; and 3) improve water use.behaviors, including increased household use of basic water sources, decreased.financial barriers to water access, and increased participation of women and.marginalized groups in community decision-making related to water access and.management. The activity will use training and technical assistance for water.service providers to ensure the quality and continuity of services, and will.construct, repair, and rehabilitate small-water distribution systems in the.targeted counties. The $3 million of funding allocated to this IM contributes.to meeting the required water earmark..</narrative>
  </description>
